  "body": "**Blocked by:** none\n\n## Context\nReview of pull request #439 found that the doc comment on `backend/packages/data/src/agentRuns/agentRunsStore.ts` (currently around lines 82-89) states `userId` is \"required for a user-triggered root\", but `backend/packages/agent-runtime/src/sempConversation.ts` (lines 159-164) creates a `triggeredBy: \"user\"` root run without passing `userId`, silently relying on the store's `getEarliestUserId` fallback instead. The doc comment therefore misstates the actual, already-accepted behavior.\n\n## Task\n- Update the doc comment on the relevant function/parameter in `backend/packages/data/src/agentRuns/agentRunsStore.ts` (currently around lines 82-89) to accurately describe that `userId` is optional even for a `triggeredBy: \"user\"` root run, and that when omitted, the store falls back to `getEarliestUserId`.\n\n## Touches\n- backend/packages/data/src/agentRuns/agentRunsStore.ts (the doc comment named above only)\n\n## Scope\n### In scope\n- The wording of the named doc comment.\n\n### Out of scope\n- The `getEarliestUserId` fallback behavior itself, and `sempConversation.ts`'s call site.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- The doc comment no longer states `userId` is required for a user-triggered root run, and instead describes the actual fallback behavior.\n\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=439 key=0b0012331d -->",
